{"id":3923,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/can-cant/","parentId":540,"order":100,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Can, can’t: Ability, possibility, permission","seo":{"title":"Can, can't: Ability, possibility, permission - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use 'can' and 'can't' in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Can-cannot.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T10:47:32","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct option to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"450\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Write affirmative (+) and negative (-) sentences using <em>can, can’t</em> with the words below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"451\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete this job interview with <em>can, can’t</em> and the words in brackets.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"452\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Can, can’t:&nbsp;Grammar chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18633\" src=\"/media/uploads/can-cannot_form-use.jpg\" alt=\"Grammar chart displaying the form and use of modal verbs 'can' and 'can't' for expressing ability, permission, and possibility, with correct and incorrect example sentences.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Can, can’t:&nbsp;Form</h2> <h4>Infinitive without <strong>to</strong></h4> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>can</strong> +&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/verbs-infinitive-verbs-ing/\">infinitive</a>&nbsp;</strong>without&nbsp;<strong>to</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>can swim</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>can to swim</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>We <strong><span>can’t come</span></strong>.</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>can’t to come</strong></span>.</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Don’t use <strong>-s</strong> after <strong>he/she/it</strong></h4> <p>We don’t add <strong>-s</strong> after&nbsp;<strong>he/she/it</strong>.&nbsp;We use&nbsp;<strong>can</strong> for all persons.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>He <span><strong>can</strong></span> swim. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>cans</strong></span> swim. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Don’t use <strong>do/don’t</strong></h4> <p><strong>Can</strong> is an auxiliary verb and has a negative and interrogative form. We don’t use&nbsp;<strong>do/don’t</strong> to make questions and negatives.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><strong><span>Can</span></strong> you swim? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em><strong><span>Do</span></strong> you <span><strong>can</strong></span> swim? <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>He <span><strong>can’t</strong></span> swim. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>He <strong><span>don’t can</span></strong>&nbsp;swim. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h2>Can, can’t:&nbsp;Use</h2> <h4>Ability</h4> <p>We use <strong>can/can’t</strong> to talk about <strong>ability</strong> in the present (=things that we know how to do).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Laura <span><strong>can sing</strong> </span>very well.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>can’t speak</strong></span> German.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>Possibility</h4> <p>We use <strong>can/can’t</strong> to ask for <strong>permission</strong> or to say if something is <strong>possible</strong> or not.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Can</strong></span> I sit here?</em></li> <li><em>You <span><strong>can’t vote</strong></span> if you aren’t 18 years old.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I’m sorry, but I <span><strong>can’t come</strong></span> to the party.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>Ask for something</h4> <p>We use <strong>can/can’t</strong> to <strong>ask for something</strong> and to <strong>order</strong> in bars, restaurants, shops, etc.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Can you lend</strong></span> me some money?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Can I have</strong></span> some water, please?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Can I have</strong></span> a burger and a soda?</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":450,"questions":[{"id":3920,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> ask you a question?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["I can","Can I","Do I can"]}]},{"id":3921,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. The music is too loud.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["can't to hear","don't can hear","can't hear"]}]},{"id":3925,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'Can you play the piano?' 'Yes, I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["play","can","do"]}]},{"id":3922,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> four languages.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["can speaks","can speak","cans speak"]}]},{"id":3923,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He says that he <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> me. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["can't helps","can't help","can't to help"]}]},{"id":3924,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a ham and cheese pizza, please?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Do I can have","Can I have","Can I to have"]}]},{"id":3926,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'Can I smoke here?' 'No, you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't","can't","aren't"]}]},{"id":3927,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> use our phones in class.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't can","can't to","cannot"]}]},{"id":3928,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> my car if he needs it. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["can use","cans use","can to use"]}]},{"id":3929,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the window, please?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Do you can open","Can you to open","Can you open"]}]}]},{"id":451,"questions":[{"id":3930,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She / dance / very well. ⇒ She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.&nbsp; <strong>(+)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3931,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I / finish / the composition for tomorrow. ⇒ I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> for tomorrow.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3932,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You / park / your car here. ⇒ You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> here.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3933,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Jim / come / to the concert with us. ⇒ Jim <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> with us.&nbsp; <strong>(+)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3934,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She / meet / you at 7. ⇒ She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3935,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You / use / this app to view documents. ⇒ You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to view documents. &nbsp; <strong>(+)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3936,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We / lose / this match. ⇒ We <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3937,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>They / understand / my decision. ⇒ They <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3938,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She / stay / at my house tonight. ⇒ She <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> tonight.&nbsp; <strong>(+)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3939,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You / see / the sea from the balcony. ⇒ You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> from the balcony.&nbsp; <strong>(-)</strong></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":452,"questions":[{"id":3940,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Interviewer: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/drive)?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3941,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Ann: Yes, I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. I have a driving license and a car. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3942,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Interviewer: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/accept) criticism?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3943,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Ann: I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (not accept) negative criticism, but I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> (accept) constructive criticism. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3944,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Interviewer: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/use) the Microsoft Office Suite?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3945,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Ann: Yes, I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. I have a lot of experience using Word, Excel, and PowerPoint.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3946,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Interviewer: <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (speak) German or French? </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3947,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Ann: I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (speak) German very well, but I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> (not speak) French very fluently. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3948,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Interviewer: When <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (you/start)?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3949,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Ann: I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (be) here tomorrow morning if you want. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}